== 2026-11-20 18:20:48 AMENDMENT 5, reported to the coordinator. It was written AFTER lane A's first Windows-made row (winb's D 17) had started at
17:31:06 under the old rule: that row printed "NOT the record system" for |F| 2.2770621748e-10 against 2.2759514360e-10 (4.9e-4 relative)
at equal steps (2744), and it runs on; its check is read under this amendment from those printed values. Every later row uses it.
The system check "|F| within 1e-6 relative of the record's F" cannot hold across machines. winb's signtest batch rebuilt Mac-made records
with |F| off by 1.5e-4 to 1.3e-3 relative at equal step counts (raw I1025-win/signtest_lowD/signtest_lowD.jsonl, D 10.5-14.5): that is
the BLAS and FFT rounding of the residual. So the 1e-6 rule would reject every Windows-made record on the Mac: D 15 (win2c), 15.5 (win2c),
16.25 (win2b), 16.5, 16.75, 17 (winb). That rejection would be about the platform, not the discrete system.
The check becomes signtest.py's (signtest_lowD_preflight.log): steps equal, and |F - F_record| <= max(1e-2 F_record, 1e-13). Its control
fired there: D 5 with the wrong u0/Ks/kappa gave F 1e5x off and other steps. The Mac-made rows already run (Fb D 16) pass both forms.
p4_hybrid.py prints both F values and the steps for every row, so the old rule can still be read from the logs.
